{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q27ZiPn27r4cpsaJrzx91C","type":"tool_result","content":"# MXFS — Success Criteria\n\nThis is the ship gate for MXFS.  Each criterion below has a concrete\nverifier script under `tests/criteria/`.  Each script prints one line:\n\n```\nRESULT: PASS  criterion=<name>  measured=<value>  threshold=<value>\nRESULT: FAIL  criterion=<name>  measured=<value>  threshold=<value>  reason=...\n```\n\nExit 0 = PASS, nonzero = FAIL.\n\n## ⚠️ SHIP-GATE CONTRACT — READ BEFORE STOPPING\n\n**The ship gate is `tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh`.  MXFS is not ready\nto ship — and the work is not done — until `verify_ship.sh` exits 0\nin a single end-to-end run with every criterion PASSing.**\n\n### The work loop\n\n1. **The model cannot self-declare done.**  This document is the\n   only authority.  Until `verify_ship.sh` exits 0 (every criterion\n   PASS, no skips), the work continues.  CLAUDE.md Rule 1 binds:\n   no handoff, no final summary, no \"wrap up\" while any criterion\n   is failing.  The CC-loop harness will keep re-invoking the model\n   (\"get back to work\") until the gate is green; the model should\n   not try to slip past the loop with framings like \"good place to\n   pause\" or \"next-session priorities.\"\n\n2. **After any code change (bug fix, refactor, perf tweak):**\n   immediately re-run the specific criterion that failed (or that\n   the change targets).  Do not re-run the whole gate yet — that\n   turns every fix into a 30-minute re-verify cycle.  Run the one\n   relevant criterion script directly, e.g.\n   `./tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh`.\n\n3. **Iterate down the failed-criteria list.**  When the targeted\n   criterion turns green, move to the next failing one.  Fix it,\n   re-run that one only, repeat.  You do NOT need to re-run\n   already-passing criteria mid-iteration — the fast feedback loop\n   per criterion is the whole point.\n\n4. **The final gate, before declaring done:**  run\n   `./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh` end-to-end.  Every criterion\n   must PASS in that single run.  No partial credit, no \"passes\n   except for X,\" no skips.  If any criterion fails in the final\n   gate run — even one that passed in isolation earlier — you go\n   back to step 2.  A fix in one area can regress another;\n   end-to-end greenness is the only valid stopping condition.\n\n5. **A criterion FAIL is real until proven otherwise.**  Default\n   assumption: the FAIL reflects a real problem in MXFS (kernel\n   module, userspace tool, on-disk format, or test infra under\n   `tests/`).  Only modify the criterion script itself when you've\n   confirmed the criterion as written is wrong — e.g., it tests a\n   feature that doesn't exist, or its threshold is fundamentally\n   inconsistent with the architecture.  Loosening a threshold to\n   make a real failure pass is never the right move.\n\n## Persistent state: `.criteria_results.json`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21180450-bea3-4db1-90da-9f0a93d0bb8c","uuid":"bc5276a1-b0c3-4477-a7c3-6fa35ee1e0f0","timestamp":"2026-06-11T04:00:40.733Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# MXFS — Success Criteria\n\nThis is the ship gate for MXFS.  Each criterion below has a concrete\nverifier script under `tests/criteria/`.  Each script prints one line:\n\n```\nRESULT: PASS  criterion=<name>  measured=<value>  threshold=<value>\nRESULT: FAIL  criterion=<name>  measured=<value>  threshold=<value>  reason=...\n```\n\nExit 0 = PASS, nonzero = FAIL.\n\n## ⚠️ SHIP-GATE CONTRACT — READ BEFORE STOPPING\n\n**The ship gate is `tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh`.  MXFS is not ready\nto ship — and the work is not done — until `verify_ship.sh` exits 0\nin a single end-to-end run with every criterion PASSing.**\n\n### The work loop\n\n1. **The model cannot self-declare done.**  This document is the\n   only authority.  Until `verify_ship.sh` exits 0 (every criterion\n   PASS, no skips), the work continues.  CLAUDE.md Rule 1 binds:\n   no handoff, no final summary, no \"wrap up\" while any criterion\n   is failing.  The CC-loop harness will keep re-invoking the model\n   (\"get back to work\") until the gate is green; the model should\n   not try to slip past the loop with framings like \"good place to\n   pause\" or \"next-session priorities.\"\n\n2. **After any code change (bug fix, refactor, perf tweak):**\n   immediately re-run the specific criterion that failed (or that\n   the change targets).  Do not re-run the whole gate yet — that\n   turns every fix into a 30-minute re-verify cycle.  Run the one\n   relevant criterion script directly, e.g.\n   `./tests/criteria/zero_silent_loss.sh`.\n\n3. **Iterate down the failed-criteria list.**  When the targeted\n   criterion turns green, move to the next failing one.  Fix it,\n   re-run that one only, repeat.  You do NOT need to re-run\n   already-passing criteria mid-iteration — the fast feedback loop\n   per criterion is the whole point.\n\n4. **The final gate, before declaring done:**  run\n   `./tests/criteria/verify_ship.sh` end-to-end.  Every criterion\n   must PASS in that single run.  No partial credit, no \"passes\n   except for X,\" no skips.  If any criterion fails in the final\n   gate run — even one that passed in isolation earlier — you go\n   back to step 2.  A fix in one area can regress another;\n   end-to-end greenness is the only valid stopping condition.\n\n5. **A criterion FAIL is real until proven otherwise.**  Default\n   assumption: the FAIL reflects a real problem in MXFS (kernel\n   module, userspace tool, on-disk format, or test infra under\n   `tests/`).  Only modify the criterion script itself when you've\n   confirmed the criterion as written is wrong — e.g., it tests a\n   feature that doesn't exist, or its threshold is fundamentally\n   inconsistent with the architecture.  Loosening a threshold to\n   make a real failure pass is never the right move.\n\n## Persistent state: `.criteria_results.json`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
